            <ArticleTitle>Diffuse idiopathic skeletal hyperostosis (DISH): where we are now and where to go next.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e000472</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/rmdopen-2017-000472</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diffuse idiopathic skeletal hyperostosis (DISH) is a well-recognised entity characterised by calcifications and ossifications of the entheses affecting mainly the spine and peripheral sites. DISH is still insufficiently investigated and understood. The objective of this report is to highlight the present limitations of our understanding of the condition and suggest future research paths.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
